# Who may sign release tags (docs/release.md, "Signed release tags").
#
# publish-release refuses a tag v<version> unless it is SSH-signed by a key
# listed here for the tag's tagger email (.github/scripts/check-tag-signature.py,
# main's copy of this file). One line per key, in ssh-keygen(1)
# ALLOWED SIGNERS format, restricted to git signatures:
#
#   <email> namespaces="git" <key type> <public key> [comment]
#
# The email is the one `git config user.email` sets when the human tags; it
# must match exactly (no patterns). Optional valid-after="YYYYMMDD" and
# valid-before="YYYYMMDD" bound a key's life; to revoke a key, delete its line
# or set valid-before. Changes go through a pull request a human merges
# (.github/ is a controlled path).
#
# No signer is listed yet, so every tag is refused until one is added.
